SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Patitiri
LOCATION:Patitiri\, Alonnisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agia Paraskevi is the patroness of Alonnisos and her church is in Patitiri\, the port: on the evening of 25 July there is a great vespers and a procession of the icon through the streets and along the harbour\, and the municipality's panigiri follows on the quay with a traditional orchestra (the Verykokkos family violins in 2025) and dancing until the early hours. Liturgy next morning. It is the island's biggest night after 15 August\; ferries arrive right into the party\, so book a room in Patitiri or Votsi.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#patitiri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-patitiri
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#patitiri-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-patitiri
